title: Classroom MVP wave 1 SHIPPED — the failure→reinforcement loop turns
summary: 'Wave 1 of the Classroom MVP is built + verified + committed (f55b25e6, branch classroom-mvp). The learning-loop core works end-to-end: a certified learning that breaks in the field (reviewer/human dismissed/revised verdict) is attributed back via the orchestrationId join to the entry that caused it, its appliedAndBrokeCount is bumped, confidence is revised DOWN (latest-wins/no-ratchet), and its classroom-certification flips pending→overturned. Guards proven: anti-grief (can''t blame an entry never loaded) + durable dedupe (one revision per entryId+orchestrationId, seeded from the field-failures ledger). The reducer runs at ambient postflight in production (import bug caught + fixed: ambient.ts:579 called runFieldFailureReducer with no import → would have thrown at runtime so the loop never turned; now imported). The tester found + fixed a per-invocation dedupe defect (penalty compounded across passes). 90 tests green. New: field-failures.ts (jsonl writers), field-failure-reducer.ts; changed: notebooks.ts (appliedAndBrokeCount/refinement/provenance ''external''), notebook-loader.ts (reviseDown), orchestration.ts (orchestrationId threading), nomination-engine.ts (cert at promotion), ambient.ts (postflight wiring). Wave 2 next: .syllabus + scenario bank + the two skills + doctor repeat-failure-rate metric.'
